  "slug": "zero-dna-mirrordna-8a09",
  "summary": "New preprints stress-test variant predictors, virtual knock-outs and Open Targets scoring, finding several comparisons undecided or non-causal.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is critical evaluation of computational evidence used to nominate causal genes and variants. At the gene level, zero-shot virtual knock-out rankings from observational single-cell data track network out-degree rather than causal gene effects. An Open Targets re-ranking for Alzheimer and Parkinson disease separates genetic from protein evidence channels, improving curated-gene recall in an auditable way. At the variant level, Manski sharp bounds that account for unscored variants show that many comparisons of variant effect predictors on ClinVar and published benchmarks cannot be decided, including comparisons involving Evo 2. A benchmark of six genomic foundation models on LGMD-gene ClinVar variants ranks Evo2 strongest at 501 bp context and evaluates adaptation strategies. SpliceVarMech instead proposes a causal generative framework for non-canonical splicing variants. The new element is quantifying when evidence is uninformative, through bounds, null-like baselines and channel separation, rather than reporting headline accuracy alone.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
